sec.p:
We passaged L. musarum under four temperatures (20°C, 25°C, 30°C and 25°C–35°C heatwave) and two infection treatments (hosts present and environmental [no‐host] controls) (Figure 2A). At each temperature, we independently passaged six replicate host‐evolved populations (24 populations total), and three replicate environmental control populations (n = 12). Our unit of biological replication was each independently evolving bacterial population. We ran the experiment for ten passages, equating to ten host generations. All in vitro culturing of L. musarum was conducted at a common temperature (25°C), OP50 at 30°C, and all nematode maintenance at 20°C (optimal for 
C. elegans
), to minimise and standardise laboratory selection.
